usb-lcd-dashboard (0.11.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Auto-detect the attached panel and restore a separately saved layout for
    each serial or TURZX device, for laptops moving between desks and KVMs.
  * Keep Claude session and weekly limit meters synchronized with the OAuth
    usage endpoint when status-line updates are quiet.
  * Add a Linux notification-area icon, matching the Windows tray.
  * Drive current-generation TURZX USB panels on Linux: ship the raw-USB udev
    rule and depend on python3-usb and python3-pycryptodome.
  * Make display.kind="auto" pick the transport from the configured size
    instead of always choosing the serial panel.
  * Reconnect TURZX panels that leave the bus, as a KVM switch does.
  * Report the attached panel and its /dev/bus/usb node in doctor.
  * Rework the settings editor: the tile canvas stays on screen, the live
    panel and per-widget settings move into tabs, screen-wide settings
    collapse into one panel, and Discord, notification and todo settings
    now appear with the widget that uses them.

 -- USB LCD Dashboard <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:40:00 +0000

